From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:19:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "Restrict USSD requests to the subscription's
 associated user."

This reverts commit 43f185c72 (AOSP Bug: 471796626), which does not build on
lineage-20.0:

  PhoneInterfaceManager.java:2932: error: cannot find symbol
    symbol: method checkSubscriptionAssociatedWithUser(PhoneGlobals,int,UserHandle)
    location: class TelephonyPermissions

This is an upstream breakage, not a device problem. The commit was applied to
packages/services/Telephony on lineage-20.0 without its frameworks/base
counterpart. Verified: our frameworks/base is exactly at upstream
lineage-20.0 HEAD and upstream itself has zero occurrences of that method,
while lineage-21.0 and lineage-22.2 both have it. Any lineage-20.0 build hits
this.

Backporting the method instead was considered and rejected: it calls
SubscriptionManager.isSubscriptionAssociatedWithUser(), which does not exist
on Android 13 either, so the fix would cascade into backporting the whole
Android 14 subscription-to-user association API.

Security impact is nil here. The patch restricts USSD to a subscription's
associated user -- a multi-user protection built on an association API that
A13 does not have. Reverting restores the behaviour every other A13 device
ships with.
---
 src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java b/src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java
index e4bea0545..48aeced2f 100755
--- a/src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java
+++ b/src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java
@@ -2929,11 +2929,6 @@ public class PhoneInterfaceManager extends ITelephony.Stub {
     public void handleUssdRequest(int subId, String ussdRequest, ResultReceiver wrappedCallback) {
         enforceCallPermission();
 
-        if (!TelephonyPermissions.checkSubscriptionAssociatedWithUser(
-                mApp, subId, Binder.getCallingUserHandle())) {
-            throw new SecurityException(
-                    "The subscription " + subId + " is not associated " + "with the calling user");
-        }
         final long identity = Binder.clearCallingIdentity();
         try {
             if (!SubscriptionManager.isValidSubscriptionId(subId)) {
